US-053 is implemented and its tests pass on Linux (clang) and Windows, but I did not mark it complete. The `linux-gcc` gate can't run here, the acceptance benchmark has no target yet, and the terrain and streamer wiring is not done. I followed the US-052 precedent and left the story Partial, with no COMPLETE signal. Nothing was committed.

**What was built** (in `engine/physics/`):
- **Shapes:** capsule, convex hull, mesh, and heightfield colliders, alongside box and sphere. Mesh and heightfield are static-only.
- **Filters and triggers:** each body has a 32-bit layer and mask, and a pair collides only when each side's mask includes the other's layer. A trigger reports contacts and is found by queries, but does not push bodies.
- **Queries:** `raycast` and `shape_cast` return the nearest hit with its entity, world position, normal, distance, and trigger flag. A `QueryFilter` selects by layer, can skip triggers, and can ignore one entity.
- **Collider replacement:** `replace_collider` swaps the shape of a live body and keeps its id and pose.
- **Streamed cells:** `CollisionCells` loads and unloads a cell's bodies. An unload waits while a dynamic or kinematic body is in the cell's footprint plus a 4 m margin, at any height, so a body falling toward the cell keeps its colliders.

**Choices I made:**
- Filtering uses a per-body object-layer table, not Jolt's group filters.
- The cell check ignores height, so a falling body holds its cell.
- Mesh and heightfield colliders are rejected on dynamic bodies.

**Tests:** a new `tests/src/physics_query_tests.cpp` adds 9 cases. They cover nearest-hit raycasts, layer filtering, collision masks, triggers, every new shape, invalid descriptions, shape casts, collider replacement, queries before and after an origin rebase, and cell unload.

**Gate results:**
- **Linux:** vendor validation, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, and `linux-unit` (22 of 22) all pass.
- **Linux ASan/UBSan:** the build passes. The first `linux-sanitize` run had one failure, `platform_x11_input_tests.cpp:437`, a keyboard-focus test that my notes list as flaky. The ASan integration suite rerun passed with no sanitizer reports. I did not rerun the full sanitize ctest.
- **Windows:** vendor validation, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, and `win-unit` (21 of 21) all pass. I checked the build log, and the new sources compiled and `engine_tests.exe` relinked.

**Not done:**
- `linux-gcc`: the local GCC 9.4 cannot build Jolt, which needs GCC 11+. This needs the GCC 11 environment or CI.
- `engine_bench --suite acceptance`: no benchmark target exists yet (US-074).
- Terrain and streaming: the heightfield collider accepts any grid of heights, but nothing yet feeds it from US-047 terrain tiles, and `CollisionCells` is not connected to the engine's streamer.

**Files:** `physics_world.hpp/.cpp`, `collision_cells.hpp/.cpp` (new), `engine/physics/CMakeLists.txt`, `physics_query_tests.cpp` (new), `tests/CMakeLists.txt`. I also appended a US-053 entry and Codebase Patterns bullets to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`, and updated the physics memory note.
